[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-insulation-installation-decision :authorize-insulation-installation :proceed-with-insulation-installation :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-site-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799007112-cloud-itonami-isco-7112-bricklayers-coverage" "2799007113-cloud-itonami-isco-7113-stonemasons-coverage" "2799007114-cloud-itonami-isco-7114-concrete-placers-coverage" "2799007119-cloud-itonami-isco-7119-building-frame-trades-coverage" "2799007121-cloud-itonami-isco-7121-roofers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the insulation installation" "proceed with the insulation installation work" "finalize the insulation installation decision" "authorize the insulation installation" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override site safety officer judgment" "override safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007124, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :construction/insulation-crew-site-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:worker-verified :site-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7124", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007124: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7124 Insulation Workers job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7124\n-- Insulation Workers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout. Wave0/Wave1/Wave2 of the occupation-actor track are all 100%\ncomplete; Wave3 batch1 (7111/7112/7113/7114/7119/7121) had already\nlanded before this ADR, alongside several other Wave3 entries\n(5411/5413, 7115/7126, 8311/8312/8321/8341/8344/8350,\n9311/9331/9332) from concurrent sibling agents in the same rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id 7124 ...}` entry was\nverified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M -e\n\"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7124\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Insulation Workers\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]`, `:optional-technologies []` and `:operating-states\n[:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit]`, and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7124` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7124` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nInsulation Workers install thermal/acoustic insulation materials on\nactive job sites -- real physical-safety stakes: fiber/particulate\nexposure, confined-space work, and ventilation hazards. The\ncontrolling constraint for this vertical is that the closed op\nallowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes an\ninsulation-installation-execution decision, or overrides a site\nsafety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard\npermanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible.\nThis actor is deliberately scoped to JOB-SITE SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS\nCOORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs insulation-installation work\nitself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE, the domain\nfield-naming pattern (`:worker-id` in place of a role-specific\nidentifier), and the closed-allowlist + independently-verified-\nprovenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set: README, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\nCONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later),\nSECURITY.md, docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md,\nblueprint.edn) -- cloned and read in full this session, same\nwave/domain shape, just landed.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7124` as an OSS job-site\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for insulation workers,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Insulation Crew Advisor\n⊣ InsulationCrewGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger. All source is\nportable `.cljc` (no JVM interop); tests are `clojure.test` `.clj`,\nmatching the reference repo's own layout.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **job-site scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct insulation-installation-execution authority** -- it\nmust NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising an insulation-installation-execution decision, or any\noverride of a site safety officer's judgment. These are not merely\ngated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a particulate-exposure/\n  confined-space/ventilation concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- insulation-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** an\ninsulation-installation-execution decision or a site-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-insulation-installation-decision` cannot even be\nproposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for`\nfunctions only ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any\ncode path (a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving\nfork) ever produced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD\ncheck (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A\nsecond, independent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops\n(`insulationcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-insulation-installation-decision`,\n`:authorize-insulation-installation`,\n`:proceed-with-insulation-installation`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-site-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`insulationcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-insulation-installation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-insulation-installation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-insulation-installation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Site unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered job site (`:no-site`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/site\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with, or\n   authorizing, insulation installation, or overriding a site safety\n   officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks insulation-installation-execution/safety-\n   override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a particulate-exposure/\n  confined-space/ventilation observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  insulation-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike an\n  insulation-installation-execution or safety-officer-override\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"insulation\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a job-site coordination actor working\nadjacent to insulation-installation work necessarily discusses\n\"insulation\" and \"safety officer\" concepts to do its\nscheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`insulationcrew.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\ninsulation installation\", \"override the site safety officer's\njudgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never\nbare nouns, and\n`insulationcrew.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for insulation\ntask ...\", \"... routed for site safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`insulationcrew.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand\n`insulationcrew.actor-test/holds-an-override-site-safety-officer-judgment-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id 7124 ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7124` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7124`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this\n  same batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 23 tests, 50 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-equivalent AGPL-3.0 text to the\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7111` reference's LICENSE, sourced from GitHub's\n  own agpl-3.0 license template at repo-creation time),\n  docs/business-model.md, docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-insulation-installation` that\n  is merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize an\n  insulation-installation-execution decision exists in the code path\n  and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision with real\n  physical-safety stakes (fiber/particulate exposure, confined-space\n  work, ventilation hazards), the capability itself must not exist.\n  The only op related to site-safety escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/site-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers an insulation-installation decision for later automatic\n  execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold insulation-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the insulation-installation-\n  execution/safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional\n  block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"insulation\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses insulation\n  and safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so a\n  bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `site` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered site)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/site record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND site\n   (`:no-worker`/`:no-site`). Not an insulation-installation-execution\n   or safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry an insulation-installation-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   whether or how insulation installation proceeds -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a particulate-exposure/\n   confined-space/ventilation concern to a human/site safety officer;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the site safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- insulation-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not an insulation-installation-\n   execution or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\nan insulation-installation-execution decision or a site-safety-officer-\njudgment override -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`insulationcrew.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`insulationcrew.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`insulationcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-insulation-installation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-insulation-installation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-insulation-installation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-site-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`insulationcrew.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with insulation installation or override a\nsite safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`insulationcrew.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-site-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-17", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 23, :assertions 50, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Insulation Crew Site Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :site-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7124", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7124", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7124], :test/simulator :insulationcrew.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7124 — Insulation Workers Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7124}]
